    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required de-duplicating a computed `customerCode` on collision by appending `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2`.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `DeduplicateCustomerCode.java` (one small method):\n- Collects existing owners' codes into a `Set`, then increments `n` from 2 until `base-<n>` is free, and stores the result on the owner.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 inserted a single `dedupeCode` step in `owners.POST.yml` between `assignCode` and `countNamesakes`, so it runs after `AssignCustomerCode` computes the base and before persistence, under the same transaction.\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\nI deliberately **did not touch** `AssignCustomerCode`: that class already carries helper complexity (`hash8`, `blank`), so any edit there pays a large `WMC_other` for the whole class. Instead the new logic lives in a **fresh single-method class** (`WMC_other \u2192 1`), kept branch-light by using a `Set` for lookup (cyclomatic complexity of just the two flat loops, no nested conditionals). The only edits are one new file plus one YAML step \u2014 no existing function was modified.",
